course: dictionary
lesson: 12757
title: Describing dusk and dim colours
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dusky is a describing word. It comes from dusk, the time when evening turns into night. So when something is dusky, it is rather dark, like the light at dusk. «The dusky sky turned from orange to grey as the sun went down.» The sky is getting dark, so dusky means rather dark.
explain: Dusky can also describe a colour that is dim, not bright. «She wore a dusky blue scarf.» The scarf is a soft, dark shade of blue, not a bright one. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Dusky means rather dark, as at dusk.
fact: «Dusky» can describe a dim, dark colour, as in «dusky blue» or «dusky pink».
fact: Animals are sometimes named with this word, such as the dusky dolphin and the dusky shark.
fact: Old books sometimes used «dusky» to describe people's skin. This use is hurtful today, so never use it that way.
exercise: «The dusky sky turned from orange to grey as the sun went down.» What does dusky mean here? | *Rather dark, as at dusk | Very loud | Cold and wet | Bright and sunny
exercise: «She wore a dusky blue scarf.» What does dusky tell you about the scarf? | Bright and shiny | *A dim, dark shade of blue | Very long | Made of wool
exercise: «The children saw a dusky shape in the trees.» Which word is nearest in meaning to dusky? | Noisy | Sticky | *Shadowy | Bright
test: «The dusky evening was quiet and calm.» What time of day does dusky suggest? | Midday | Early morning | Lunchtime | *Evening, as night begins
test: Which animal is named with the word dusky in nature lessons? | The golden eagle | *The dusky dolphin | The snowy owl | The red fox
exam: «The dusky pink dress glowed in the dim light.» What does dusky mean in this sentence? | Brand new | *A dim, soft shade of pink | Dark brown and muddy | Very loud
